                        ],
                        "form": "blini"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5ca7a574-8a1b-3b0b-9047-cc4f26ee386a",
                        "entry_id": "4ea4aa7c-13e9-38b1-b566-bf68028ca128",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petite crêpe épaisse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Très rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5484985c-c491-48cb-b9ef-bb36a74095f3",
                                "sense_id": "5ca7a574-8a1b-3b0b-9047-cc4f26ee386a",
                                "text": "Graisser avec un chiffon imprégné d'huile puis verser une louche moyenne pour chaque blini, en étalant légèrement la pâte avec le dos de la louche pour réaliser un blin pas trop épais d'environ 15 cm de diamètre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fdd3080-5ee6-447a-be26-47a5f4801e26",
                                "sense_id": "5ca7a574-8a1b-3b0b-9047-cc4f26ee386a",
                                "text": "Savez-vous manger le blin à la mode de Russie ? Là-bas c'est avec de la crème aigre ou du beurre fondu que l'on sert cette petite crêpe salée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90cd6cee-752e-4948-9294-2852abeecc29",
                                "sense_id": "5ca7a574-8a1b-3b0b-9047-cc4f26ee386a",
                                "text": "Quand un côté du blin est bien doré, retournez-le et faites-le frire de l'autre côté. déposer les blinis frits les uns sur les autres sur une assiette plate. Servez les blinis avec de la confiture, de la crème épaisse ou ils peuvent également être remplis de viande, de fromage cottage, de fromage ou de caviar. le premier blin tourne toujours mal."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "732dd3b7-fe86-4dea-ba68-60cf0f082d04",
                        "source_entry_id": "4ea4aa7c-13e9-38b1-b566-bf68028ca128",
                        "source_sense_id": "5ca7a574-8a1b-3b0b-9047-cc4f26ee386a",
                        "target_lang_word": "blin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "blin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a9c6eecf-c686-3410-9ea4-8395dc8c8972",
                                        "entry_id": "61c4cce8-0add-387a-b812-ec90b7e9ffed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cease (from); to stop; to desist, to let up."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "Yorkshire",
                                            "especially",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3946685-3374-40e5-82ae-138f1aea858e",
                                                "sense_id": "a9c6eecf-c686-3410-9ea4-8395dc8c8972",
                                                "text": "nathemore for that spectacle bad, / Did th'other two their cruell vengeaunce blin [...]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb7672ae-c0f1-4c88-b00d-e21d9baa0a78",
                                                "sense_id": "a9c6eecf-c686-3410-9ea4-8395dc8c8972",
                                                "text": "One while the little foot page went, / And another while he ran; / Until he came to his journey's end / The little foot page never blan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f3b9ef6-9af7-4c44-9183-8e3b8ce897de",
                                                "sense_id": "a9c6eecf-c686-3410-9ea4-8395dc8c8972",
                                                "text": "A child may cry for half an hour, and never blin ; it may rain all day, and never blin ; the train ran 100 miles, and never blinned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "875eb435-7cce-4b72-b45d-875a921963cf",
                                                "sense_id": "a9c6eecf-c686-3410-9ea4-8395dc8c8972",
                                                "text": "Thus blinned their boast, as we well ken"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "blin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a8deaab-0558-31a2-90b5-d2ac9641c985",
                                        "entry_id": "7f468197-43ff-303a-b05b-b995cc8c8ce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cessation; end."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "blin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                        "entry_id": "7fee451d-574c-3aa5-8469-193c2abf114e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A blintz or blini."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68b866f1-a124-4d92-86d7-5fb1ffd01064",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "The cook raised an immense amount of dough for the bliny. […] “Hey, a blin for me!” one would call, holding out an empty plate with a hand dripping with butter and sour cream."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e44cf5e-ec2f-494e-9e56-36452b0953b6",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "Have a deep round buttered dish by the side of the stove and put each blin into this dish as it is ready; butter the blin, and place the next blin on top. When all the bliny are cooked, cover the dish with a cloth; it is not essential to serve them immediately."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7798c8d-0b61-4cff-b867-501948273f49",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "No one ever eats just one blin. This is probably why the singular of blini is unknown to most food aficionados, though they do know that these little thin pancakes, of either wheat or buckwheat, often accompany caviar. You wrap them around a little mound of it and dab the blin with sour cream. Royal Gourmet prepares wheat blini on order to go."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ddf5448-c61d-4711-ad91-837a0ce5e38b",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "“But Papa, art requires sacrifices,” Olenka would say, standing up for Benedikt. / “The first blin is always lumpy,” Mother-in-law comforted. / “There you go, talking about bliny again! How come you only talk about one thing: bliny and more bliny! . . .”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5ed5089-4933-4df5-98bc-a3fa4e2d9f9d",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "“I made blini for all. My grandmother’s secret recipe from Odessa.[…]” / […] “Can’t you see Jordie is hurting?” / “That’s why I offered her a blin.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4194a3a6-5d14-4370-b97f-8c48958a921b",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "Medvedev took one of the blini from Bobby’s plate, spooned red caviar onto it, rolled the blin and wolfed it down. “The secret to drinking vodka, my friend, is eating, no?” / Bobby spooned black caviar onto a blin and downed it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6abd43d5-567d-425d-af3e-5b3a4ff5a39b",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "Unlike regular pancakes, blins should be fried in a small pancake pan. This is because a good blin is thick and juicy, and this is most easily achieved using a small pan with raised edges. The blins should be fried on both sides and served hot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12c1b58f-8efe-4fe7-874d-492a6146b341",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "“Those blins have a religious origin,” Addie explained. “They are partaken of to commemorate the advent of Spring, and they are round in shape, to represent the sun.[…]” she concluded."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cc9212c-f382-4025-8560-aa3c658e2afa",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "Then tea, with his wife Lydia making blins so thin you could almost see through them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "820f90d3-7992-4fbe-b3f6-305f39d5f9a6",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "She baked some bliny. “Go, old man, and fetch your daughter for burial.” The old man rode off. The dog under the table barked: “Arf, arf! The old man’s daughter in gold and silver will come, but no groom will have the old woman’s daughter.” “Shut up, you fool! For a blin say: ‘Grooms will take the old woman’s daughter, but they’ll bring in just the bones of the old man’s daughter!’” The dog ate the blin and once more said, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3540890c-b756-45ba-9e8d-ef76e9c8b481",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "The tops of the blini should bubble up and set within 90 seconds (if they do not, then either the heat is not high enough or the pan hasn’t had time to heat up properly). Flip each blin and cook for another 90 seconds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8c5a915-86f3-439c-b144-a4026d1ecd84",
                                                "sense_id": "66fe2c4d-aa49-3497-a04c-d48fbd31bc50",
                                                "text": "“More so,” Richter replied as the waiter returned with a plate of blini topped with glistening caviar. […] She took a blin and crammed it into her mouth: the taste was overwhelming and salty, not at all what she’d expected, and not to her taste."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "58e65a58-2edf-415e-8eaf-67e9a419408f",
                        "source_entry_id": "4ea4aa7c-13e9-38b1-b566-bf68028ca128",
                        "source_sense_id": "5ca7a574-8a1b-3b0b-9047-cc4f26ee386a",
                        "target_lang_word": "bliny",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bliny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34fb9252-cfc8-31a3-b12a-3427fd0774f1",
                                        "entry_id": "60ef3637-1579-395c-b1b9-37f3e47b5992",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of blini."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "faed3575-47b9-4b0d-b0b3-e51b9a576a8c",
                                                "sense_id": "34fb9252-cfc8-31a3-b12a-3427fd0774f1",
                                                "text": "In fact, buckwheat is most popular in pancakes, on its own or mixed with wheat, as in blinys."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caf73107-d10d-4ddc-8e5c-cfca15310ae9",
                                                "sense_id": "34fb9252-cfc8-31a3-b12a-3427fd0774f1",
                                                "text": "The Chainaya, or tea-room, used to be the place for a late supper of blinys and champagne after a ballet at the Bolshoy across the street, one of the few places in town where one could hope to eat that late."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70c9d7aa-9f63-4d57-84a2-e1e858c779c3",
                                                "sense_id": "34fb9252-cfc8-31a3-b12a-3427fd0774f1",
                                                "text": "When finished with the first helping, a refill or two was automatically provided, no questions asked. It was murderous, but there was no escape. We developed a new vocabulary, all evolving around the concept of “murder by blinys,” but it didn’t take away the obligation to eat until one’s pants couldn’t fit anymore and there was difficulty walking without constant belly pains."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e03e465-b13f-4bb5-931e-ae954ed6e2f1",
                                                "sense_id": "34fb9252-cfc8-31a3-b12a-3427fd0774f1",
                                                "text": "Many of the villagers provided Mama with milk and cheese, and she made dozens and dozens of bliny for everyone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bliny",
